<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed clashes persist in Bangui as government forces, former Séléka rebels, Anti-balaka militias, Russian Wagner troops and Africa Corps continue fighting each other. The United Nations warned against a premature withdrawal of peacekeepers while Chad arrested four suspects after an attack in Miski and CAR officials denied that their forces crossed the Chad border during a raid. In the Lake Chad basin, regional troops killed 16 ISWAP fighters, including senior leader Abu Zubiru, in air and artillery strikes. The conflict caused 246 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxPSW9id3M0T01CRUtpM19JSXNpd1c4QXlCM29iQnVOaHlDT0tBajRCU2lwYzhndDRSbGJTUXdpcXBRNTR0US1BeV96S1pZMEZZa0NYM3RLU1Nuam41US1nbzRONFhxVlFZSWYzeXRwTEMySWlMUlNhaW1xRW5yaE5ab1BuSll2NG5OM3J4eUVXMVczclRIc0tWSER5cV9BcWlGVldvcjhUdnkydWxpOVdIWENldHRLZEo1RklCLUpsNEhFZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilAFBVV95cUxPeVptRXNVcHBvdHZ2bE41clh3UkU1WDJBZHh6T2VLOFF2ZlRJUVRYSGNCMGJoRThfOTlESWNHbmplVjY2cHgxX1NBTjhSaVJuaEc1N1RyajhJNXRNTGhmRTdteDdTV1F0MGdGb0tMX05iZ3R5anRIWDNIV2t0X1l5M2ZKcjd4WFVHTUh1MlNnMUtPRlNf?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Nation Newspaper&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTE9NZFdGTnhtQWpCb0prYlA1YkM3Zl9qSUxCOW92bWphb0lGVU13MVktMDM3LWtUcXA4bDZSYnp0am5rb19neWlkSHYwTzhIX0I0c1VSZ1VaQUNteEJQWnNMQzFKbmcyRVpBbVpXbGt0ZUIzT29zckE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Amnesty International&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Channels Television&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiakFVX3lxTE0yeFFuQzk0OWxkdWVkSkZCR3lnQjV5SnlZVTR5R2d2U2lTTEtKSWowenFZR21wRTlibXFBb1ppOUpqeFF0T1hh